+        `ws://127.0.0.1:${ctx.argv.wsPort}`
 
+    // Local patch: Chromium closes the socket when the Mac sleeps, and upstream
+    // never opens a new one, so the page stopped reloading. Reconnect, and reload
+    // when the server's build token differs from the one that served the page
+    // (its Server-Timing header; see quartz/cli/handlers.js). A rebuild sends a
+    // new token, and a socket that opens gets the current one. Only a UUID-shaped
+    // message becomes the baseline, for a page with no token; any other message
